.TH OROC-UPDATE-BUNDLE 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.1" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-update\-bundle \- Build a tar archive containing the contents of a directory for use as an update artifact.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc update bundle [\-\-input=<dir>] [\-\-output=<bundle.tar>] [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Build a tar archive containing the contents of a directory for use as an update artifact.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-input=<dir>\fR
directory whose contents will be archived (default: project directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-output=<bundle.tar>\fR
path to the tar archive to write (default: <build_name>\-<version>.tar)
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest=<path>\fR
optional manifest path to update with a new target for this bundle
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest\-name=<name>\fR
manifest filename to use when \-\-manifest is not provided
.TP
\fB\-\-channel=<name>\fR
update channel to associate with this bundle (default: update_channel or "stable")
.TP
\fB\-\-update\-id=<id>\fR
update id to associate with this bundle (default: <channel>\-<version>)
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<id>\fR
platform identifier for the bundle target (default: "source")
.TP
\fB\-\-arch=<id>\fR
architecture identifier for the bundle target (default: "any")
.TP
\fB\-\-artifact\-url=<url\-or\-path>\fR
artifactUrl to record in the manifest target (default: bundle filename)
.TP
\fB\-\-hash\-algorithm=<sha256|sha1>\fR
hash algorithm to use for the bundle payload (default: sha256 when libsodium is available, otherwise sha1)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.PP
The archive is a plain tar file (no compression) built using the runtime's native tar implementation. Directory layout and basic metadata (mode bits, mtime) are preserved. When omitted, '\-\-input' defaults to the project directory (app source), and '\-\-output' defaults to "<build_name>\-<version>.tar" derived from your oro.toml metadata. When '\-\-manifest' or '\-\-manifest\-name' (or ORO_UPDATE_MANIFEST_FILENAME) is provided, the manifest is updated with a new target entry describing this bundle (including length and hash).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc update bundle\fR
bundle the current project source into <build_name>\-<version>.tar
.TP
\fBoroc update bundle \-\-manifest manifest.json\fR
bundle the project and record the artifact in manifest.json
.TP
\fBoroc update bundle \-\-input dist \-\-output app\-1.2.3.tar \-\-manifest manifest.json \-\-channel beta\fR
bundle a custom directory and attach it as a beta update in the manifest
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-update(1)
